Z||000000||lennyb4||05-05-2000||03:48 PM||||I dont know what all you guys do for a living, BUT dont ever get into Quality Assurance Management. I've been doing this ****  for 10 years and im soooo tired of always cleaning up other peoples mistakes. I have decided it time for a change. If i keep doing this crap i will have to change my name to PhYsCo pretty soon.   Freek it all..<P>Sorry guys just needed to vent or id burst..||||reg||4
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||05-05-2000||04:09 PM||||I know what you mean.  I work for the Navy as a telecom consultant.  Lately I've sucked into working out a quality assurance plan for a huge new network here in Hawaii. I know nothing about quality assurance.  I've been reading through huge volumes of documents from RFPs to the contractor CDRLs and I seem to be spending longer periods of time staring into space than usual.  I really dilike this line of work and am getting bored silly trying to force myself to read all this stuff and trying to write down a document that makes sense.  I am thinking about taking some money and starting to invest on-line.  I know several people that have done this and did well enough to quit their other jobs.  Wish we had a lottery here in Hawaii.  They keep voting it down here (the Las Vegas lobby is strong here)  A huge amount of money goes to Vegas every year from here.  I'm rambling- gotta go.||||reg||8
