Z||000003||RFMike||05-06-2000||09:28 AM||||One of my jobs at an architectural firm was QA and Standards.  What a drag!  First of all, you have to be a hardass, which eventually gets old.  Then, when you finally get some nimrod to understand what you are trying to implement, and he actually becomes competent, he goes out and gets a job for 50% more money.  Start over with another warm body, fresh out of school.  <BR>Second, you have to deal with the mistakes other people make, and often take a portion of the blame.  AACCKK.<BR>I don't do that anymore, and never will again.  People where I work now actually think I'm a nice guy, at least some of the time.<BR>My advice- it takes a certain mentality to thrive at QA.  If your personality doesn't fit that profile, you need to get out of it, NOW.<BR>Good luck.<BR>Mike||||reg||1
